<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 170 0 R/T(Water Safety  Policy)/E(Water Safety  Policy)/Pg 28 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

514 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 170 0 R/Pg 28 0 R/A[1120 0 R 0]/K[2]>>
endobj

515 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 170 0 R/E(11)/Pg 28 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

516 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 170 0 R/E(       Being a beach and outdoor activity based school, water safety is treated as one of our highest priorities. Our aim is for every child to enjoy the ocean, pool, and water-based activities with confidence, while minimising risk at every stage.)/Pg 28 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

517 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1121 0 R/E(All beach, surf, and swimming activities are supervised by a qualified surf coach or teacher, at a ratio appropriate to the students' age and swimming ability, and never fewer than one adult to eight students in the water.)/Pg 28 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

518 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1122 0 R/E(A dedicated water-safety spotter, separate from the instructing coach, watches the group from the beach or poolside for the duration of any water activity.)/Pg 28 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

519 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1123 0 R/E(Students are counted in and out of the water at the start and end of every session.)/Pg 28 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

520 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 170 0 R/T(Before Water Activities)/E(Before Water Activities)/Pg 28 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

521 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1124 0 R/E(Parents must disclose any swimming ability concerns, medical conditions, or fears of water on the enrollment Medical Information form, and update the school immediately if this changes.)/Pg 28 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

522 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1125 0 R/E(Children who cannot yet swim confidently will be given a personal flotation device \(PFD\) or rash vest with built-in buoyancy for beach and surf sessions, and will remain in shallower, closely supervised areas.)/Pg 28 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

523 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1126 0 R/E(Ocean conditions \(tide, swell, and current\) are checked before every beach session; activities are adjusted, moved, or cancelled if conditions are assessed as unsafe.)/Pg 28 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

524 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 170 0 R/Pg 28 0 R/A[1127 0 R 0]/K[12]>>
endobj

525 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 170 0 R/Pg 28 0 R/A[1128 0 R 0]/K[13]>>
endobj

526 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 171 0 R/T(Equipment & Sun Safety)/E(Equipment & Sun Safety)/Pg 29 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

527 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 171 0 R/Pg 29 0 R/A[1129 0 R 0]/K[1]>>
endobj

528 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1130 0 R/E(Surfboards, leashes, and rash vests are provided and checked for safety before each session. If equipment needs to be hired, this will be an extra charge to the parents under activities cost. )/Pg 29 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

529 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1131 0 R/E(Children must wear reef-safe sunscreen and a rash vest or sun-protective clothing during water and beach activities; parents are asked to apply sunscreen before drop-off on activity days.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

530 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 171 0 R/T(Emergency Response)/E(Emergency Response)/Pg 29 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

531 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1132 0 R/E(All coaches and water-safety staff hold current CPR and water-rescue training, refreshed annually.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

532 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1133 0 R/E(In the event of an incident in the water, the nearest qualified staff member responds immediately while the group is brought to safety by the remaining supervising adults; parents are notified as soon as the child is safe.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

533 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1134 0 R/E(A stocked first aid kit and emergency contact list are kept at every beach and pool session.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

