<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 172 0 R/T(General Rule)/E(General Rule)/Pg 30 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

538 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 172 0 R/T(Medication  Policy)/E(Medication  Policy)/Pg 30 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

539 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 172 0 R/Pg 30 0 R/A[1137 0 R 0]/K[2]>>
endobj

540 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 172 0 R/E(12)/Pg 30 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

541 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 172 0 R/E(      The safe handling of medication is taken seriously at Selong Bay School. The following policy applies to all students, whether on campus for a full day or attending an activity session.)/Pg 30 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

542 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 172 0 R/E(No medication \204 prescription, over-the-counter, or herbal/homeopathic \204 will be given to a student by school staff without prior written permission from a parent or guardian. Students, including older students, may not carry or self-administer medication on campus without this written authorisation, with the exception of clearly agreed emergency medication \(see below\).)/Pg 30 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

543 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 172 0 R/T(Giving the School Permission to Administer Medication)/E(Giving the School Permission to Administer Medication)/Pg 30 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

544 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1138 0 R/E(Parents must complete and sign a Medication Authorisation Form, stating the child's name, the medication, dosage, timing, and reason for use.)/Pg 30 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

545 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1139 0 R/E(All medication must be provided in its original, labelled packaging with the child's name clearly marked, and handed directly to a staff member \204 never left in a school bag or lunchbox.)/Pg 30 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

546 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1140 0 R/E(The school keeps a written log of every dose administered, including the time given and the staff member who administered it, and this is shared with parents on request.)/Pg 30 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

547 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1141 0 R/E(Medication is stored securely, out of children's reach, and any medication requiring refrigeration is kept in a dedicated, clearly labelled area of the staff fridge.)/Pg 30 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

548 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 172 0 R/Pg 30 0 R/A[1142 0 R 0]/K[11]>>
endobj

549 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 172 0 R/Pg 30 0 R/A[1143 0 R 0]/K[12]>>
endobj

550 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 173 0 R/T(Emergency & Ongoing Medication)/E(Emergency & Ongoing Medication)/Pg 31 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

551 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 173 0 R/Pg 31 0 R/A[1144 0 R 0]/K[1]>>
endobj

552 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1145 0 R/E(Children with a diagnosed condition requiring emergency medication \(for example, an EpiPen for severe allergy, or an inhaler for asthma\) must have an individual Health Care Plan on file, agreed with parents before the child's first day, describing the condition, triggers, and exact steps staff should take.)/Pg 31 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

553 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1146 0 R/E(Emergency medication for these students is kept close at hand \204 not locked away \204 so it can be accessed immediately, and relevant staff are briefed on how to recognise and respond to a reaction.)/Pg 31 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

554 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1147 0 R/E(If a child is unwell at school, simple analgesia may be given, such as paracetamol and ibuprofen, or anti-histamines. The school will contact the parent via WhatsApp to get approval to give the medication and the parent is required to sign the medication record upon collection of the child. )/Pg 31 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

555 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 173 0 R/T(Collecting Unused Medication)/E(Collecting Unused Medication)/Pg 31 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

556 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1148 0 R/E(Parents are asked to collect any unused or expired medication from the school at the end of a course of treatment or at the end of the school year. Medication not collected will be safely disposed of.)/Pg 31 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

557 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 173 0 R/Pg 31 0 R/A[1149 0 R 0]/K[7]>>
endobj

558 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 174 0 R/T(Sickness &  Illness Policy)/E(Sickness &  Illness Policy)/Pg 32 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

559 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 174 0 R/Pg 32 0 R/A[1150 0 R 0]/K[1]>>
endobj

560 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 174 0 R/E(13)/Pg 32 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

561 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 174 0 R/E(        We promote good health for all students and have clear guidelines for when a child should stay home. Because young children are often in close contact with one another, we ask parents to be conscientious in following this policy so we can reduce the risk of illness spreading through our school community.)/Pg 32 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

562 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 174 0 R/E(Children must stay home if they have any of the following:)/Pg 32 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

563 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1151 0 R/E(A fever of 38\260C \(100.4\260F\) or higher \204 the child must be fever-free for 24 hours without the use of fever-reducing medication before returning to school.)/Pg 32 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

564 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1152 0 R/E(Vomiting or diarrhoea within the past 24 hours \204 the child must be symptom-free for 24 hours, and for known gastric illnesses, symptom-free for 48 hours, before returning.)/Pg 32 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

565 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1153 0 R/E(An unexplained rash, conjunctivitis or other visibly contagious condition, until assessed and cleared by a doctor.)/Pg 32 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

566 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1154 0 R/E(A persistent cough, difficulty breathing, or flu-like symptoms.)/Pg 32 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

567 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1155 0 R/E(Head lice \204 a child found to have head lice will be sent home the same day for treatment, and may return once live lice are no longer present.)/Pg 32 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

568 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 174 0 R/T(If Your Child Becomes Unwell at School)/E(If Your Child Becomes Unwell at School)/Pg 32 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

569 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1156 0 R/E(If a student becomes unwell during the school day, staff will assess the child, provide first aid or comfort as needed, and contact parents if the child needs to go home or seek further medical attention. Even if a child returns to class after a minor concern, parents will be informed of the visit that day.)/Pg 32 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

